  "readmeFile": "Package.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Add: FileSystemMessageArchiveTransformer (EngineBuilder.WithFileSystemMessageArchive) and FileSystemConversationArchiveTransformer (EngineBuilder.WithFileSystemConversationArchive). Both capture every message the moment it settles, before ReasoningPruneTransformer, HistorySnipTransformer, ToolResultBudgetTransformer, or CompactionTransformer -- all before-iteration transformers -- ever get a chance to prune, truncate, or summarise it away, by registering on the after-iteration and after-turn stages instead: a multi-round tool-call turn can re-enter before-iteration (and therefore re-run pruning) within the same turn, before that turn's own after-turn pass ever fires. The message variant appends one JSON object per line -- a self-contained, immutable, per-message record, the natural shape for a future log-structured broker sink (Kafka, Event Hubs) alongside or instead of the filesystem. The conversation variant instead keeps a single growing JSON Conversation snapshot per file, the same schema FileSystemConversationPersistenceTransformer writes, rewritten atomically on every append -- for consumers that want to read a full-fidelity conversation file directly.",
